Ahh. ;) The last person you show might not be the last person who knows.

There’s a difference between seeing something, knowing what you’ve seen, and choosing to reveal it.

Sometimes the person who understands the most has the least reason to demonstrate it.

And there’s another interpretation I like:

The last person you reveal the truth to might be yourself.

Because recognizing a pattern in everyone else is one thing. Recognizing how that same pattern operates within you is another.

The observer is part of the picture, too.

And sometimes the reveal is in what you deliberately leave unseen. ;)